<rml>
<head>
	<title>Main menu</title>

	<!--
		A main menu, complete and working.

		Copy this into your own UI/screens/ and edit it. It is not meant to be linked from the plugin
		at runtime: a recipe is a starting point, not a component, and the first thing any game does is
		change it. Nothing here names Folio's directory except the library link.

		What it demonstrates, and what is worth keeping when you change everything else:
		  - one .btn-stack, so the whole menu is one navigation axis and a pad cannot get stuck
		  - autofocus on the first item, so a controller has somewhere to start
		  - data-loc on every string, so it can be translated before anyone asks
		  - not one literal colour, so it follows the theme
	-->
	<link type="text/template" href="/folio/lib/lib.rml"/>

	<style>
		body { justify-content: center; align-items: center; }

		.menu-shell { width: 420dp; }

		.brand
		{
			text-align: center;
			margin-bottom: 40dp;
		}

		.brand-sub { margin-top: 4dp; }

		.build { position: absolute; right: 24dp; bottom: 20dp; }
	</style>
</head>

<body class="screen s-pad-xl">
	<div class="menu-shell">
		<div class="brand">
			<div class="t-display c-text" data-loc="game_title">YOUR GAME</div>
			<div class="brand-sub t-caption c-dim" data-loc="game_tagline">a subtitle goes here</div>
		</div>

		<div class="btn-stack">
			<button class="btn btn-primary btn-wide focusable" id="continue" autofocus
				data-loc="menu_continue">Continue</button>
			<button class="btn btn-wide focusable" id="new_game" data-loc="menu_new">New Game</button>
			<button class="btn btn-wide focusable" id="load" data-loc="menu_load">Load Game</button>
			<button class="btn btn-wide focusable" id="settings" data-loc="menu_settings">Settings</button>
			<button class="btn btn-ghost btn-wide focusable" id="quit" data-loc="menu_quit">Quit</button>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="build t-caption c-dim" data-loc="build_label">build 0.0.0</div>
</body>
</rml>
